('500a4865-b96c-4956-bf8b-c496189b6114', 'UPPSC Prelims 2026: Complete 10-Year PYQ Analysis & Strategy', 'uppsc-prelims-10yr-pyq-analysis', '<h2>🎯 UPPSC Prelims 2026: Complete 10-Year PYQ Analysis</h2>\n<p>Data-Driven Preparation Strategy based on 10 Years of Data (2016-2025), 1,500+ Questions Analyzed, across 8 Main Subjects (150 Questions/Exam).</p>\n\n<h3>👑 Core Subject Weightages & Trends</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>History Dominates:</strong> 24 Qs/yr avg. Spectrum Modern India & NCERT Class 6-12 form the foundation.</li>\n  <li><strong>Polity is Most Stable:</strong> 22 Qs/yr avg. M. Laxmikanth covers 95% of questions. Parliament, Rights & Panchayati Raj repeat annually.</li>\n  <li><strong>Current Affairs Volatility:</strong> 22-38 Qs range. High-risk if ignored. Daily news tracking is mandatory.</li>\n  <li><strong>Geography\'s Rising Importance:</strong> 21 Qs/yr avg. Indian & World Geography. Daily 20-min atlas practice is mandatory.</li>\n  <li><strong>Science Strategy (Biology First):</strong> 19 Qs/yr avg. Biology yields 7-12 Qs. NCERT Class 9-12 coverage is sufficient.</li>\n  <li><strong>UP Special GK: Low Priority:</strong> 1-8 Qs/yr. Maximum 2% time allocation is optimal.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>📊 Subject Priority Tier Matrix</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Tier 1 (Foundation):</strong> Current Affairs (22-38 Qs), History (18-28 Qs), Indian Polity (15-27 Qs)</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier 2 (Support):</strong> Geography (18-24 Qs), General Science (17-21 Qs)</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier 3 (Final Polish):</strong> Economy & Schemes (12-15 Qs), Environment (7-10 Qs), UP Special (1-8 Qs)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>📚 Gold Standard Resource Stack</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Indian Polity:</strong> M. Laxmikanth (6th Edition)</li>\n  <li><strong>Modern History:</strong> Spectrum — Modern India</li>\n  <li><strong>Ancient & Medieval:</strong> NCERT Class 6-12 & R.S. Sharma</li>\n  <li><strong>Geography Maps:</strong> Oxford / Orient Blackswan Student Atlas (Daily 20 min)</li>\n  <li><strong>Current Affairs:</strong> Ghatnachakra Monthly / Drishti IAS Magazine</li>\n  <li><strong>Environment:</strong> Shankar IAS + ISFR State of Forest Report</li>\n</ul>', 'UPPSC Strategy', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2026-09-22 17:38:28.097', '2026-09-22 17:38:28.097'),
('dc2b370b-5cfc-4885-8904-4b0270738340', 'BPSC Syllabus and Exam Pattern 2026', 'bpsc-syllabus-exam-pattern', '<h1 style=\"color: rgb(15, 23, 42);\"><font color=\"#ee0000\" face=\"Aptos, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">BPSC SYLLABUS AND EXAM PATTERN 2026</span></font></h1><div style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><div style=\"border-width: 1.5px 1.5px 1.5px 5px; border-color: rgb(253, 230, 138) rgb(253, 230, 138) rgb(253, 230, 138) rgb(217, 119, 6); margin: 1rem 0px; padding: 1.25rem; background: rgb(255, 251, 242); border-radius: 14px;\"><blockquote style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; font-style: normal;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">About BPSC Exam</font></span></blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC) conducts the Combined Competitive Examination (CCE) every year to recruit candidates for various Group A and Group B posts under the Bihar government, including Bihar Administrative\nService (BAS), Bihar Police Service (BPS), Bihar Revenue Service (BRS) and Bihar Financial Service (BFS). If you are preparing for the BPSC exam, understanding the exact exam pattern and syllabus is the first and most important step. This article covers the complete details of all three stages of\nthe BPSC exam - Prelims, Mains, and Interview - in a simple and organized format.</span></div><p></p><blockquote style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(51, 65, 85) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\" style=\"font-style: normal;\">BPSC Selection Process:</font></span></blockquote><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px 0px 0in; line-height: normal;\"><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\">The BPSC recruitment process is completed in three stages:</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0in 0.25in; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: normal;\"></p><ol><li><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> <font color=\"#10b981\">Preliminary Examination (Prelims)</font></span> – Objective type (MCQ based) </li><li><font color=\"#10b981\" style=\"font-size: inherit;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; text-indent: -0.25in;\">Main Examination (Mains) </span>– </font>Descriptive/Objective type</li><li><font color=\"#10b981\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; text-indent: -0.25in;\">Interview</span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\"> – </span></font>Personality Test</li></ol><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px 0px 0in;\"><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px 0px 0in;\"><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">The table below gives a quick overview of all three stages:</span></font></p><table classname=\"editor-table\" style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin: 1rem 0px; width: 324.337px;\"><thead><tr style=\"background: rgb(248, 250, 252);\"><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Stage</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Type of Exam</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Total Marks</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Duration</span></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Prelims</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Objective\n(General Studies)</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">150</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">2 Hours</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Mains</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">General\nHindi (Qualifying) + GS Paper 1 + GS Paper 2 + Essay + Optional Subject\n(Qualifying)</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">1100</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">3 hours for each paper</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Interview</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Personality\nTest</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">120</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\">-</td></tr></tbody></table><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is important to note that the <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">Prelims exam is purely qualifying in nature</font></span> - its marks are not counted in the final merit list; it is only used to shortlist candidates for the Mains exam. <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">The final selection is based on the marks obtained in the Mains and Interview.</font></span></p>\n<blockquote style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(51, 65, 85) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\" style=\"font-style: normal;\">Eligibility Criteria:</font></span></blockquote><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0in 0.25in; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: normal;\"></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#10b981\">Nationality:</font></span> Indian citizen</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#10b981\">Age Limit: </font></span>Generally, 20 to 37 years (relaxation applicable as per category and post)</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\"><font color=\"#10b981\">Educational Qualification:</font></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\"> A graduate degree from a recognized university</span></li></ul><p></p><h1 style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(15, 23, 42) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">BPSC Prelims Exam Pattern:</font></span></h1><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">The Prelims exam consists of a single paper covering General Studies.</span><br><table classname=\"editor-table\" style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin: 1rem 0px; width: 284.8px;\"><thead><tr style=\"background: rgb(248, 250, 252);\"><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Detail</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Information</span></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Name\nof Exam</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Combined\nCompetitive Exam </span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">(General Studies)</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Number\nof Papers</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">1 (150 Marks)</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Mode\nof Exam</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Offline <span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px;\">(OMR based)</span>\n</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Duration</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">2 Hours</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Number\nof Questions</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">150</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Negative\nMarking</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">⅓ mark per wrong answer</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Nature\nof Questions</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Multiple-Choice\nQuestions </span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">(MCQs)</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p></p><blockquote style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(51, 65, 85) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\" style=\"font-style: normal;\">BPSC Prelims Syllabus (Subject-Wise):</font></span></blockquote><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0in 0.25in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: normal;\"></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\"> General Science: </span></span>A general understanding of science based on everyday observation and experience, along with basic questions on physics, chemistry, biology, and technological developments. No specialized subject knowledge is required.</li><li><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Current </span></span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Affairs: </span></span>Events of national and international importance, awards, sports, government schemes, and recent developments in science and technology.</li><li><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">History: </span></span>History of India and Bihar - a broad understanding of ancient, medieval, and modern Indian history, with special emphasis on Bihar.</li><li><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Geography: </span></span>Physical, social, and economic geography of India and Bihar, including Indian agriculture, natural resources, river systems, and the geographical divisions of Bihar.</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Indian </span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Polity: </span></span>India\'s            political         system, Panchayati Raj, community <span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\">development, and planning in India and Bihar.</span></li><li><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Economy: </span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\">The Indian economy and the economy of Bihar since </span>independence.</li><li><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Indian </span></span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">National Movement: </span></span>The nature and growth of nationalism in the 19th century and the role of Bihar in India\'s freedom struggle - including the Champaran Satyagraha, the Revolt of 1857, the Birsa Movement, and the Quit India Movement of 1942.</li><li><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold; color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">General </span></span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">Mental Ability: </span></span>Questions testing logical reasoning, problem-solving, and analytical ability.</li></ul><p></p></div><h1 style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(15, 23, 42) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">BPSC Mains Exam Pattern:</font></span></h1><div style=\"border-width: 1.5px 1.5px 1.5px 5px; border-color: rgb(186, 230, 253) rgb(186, 230, 253) rgb(186, 230, 253) rgb(2, 132, 199); margin: 1rem 0px; padding: 1.25rem; background: rgb(240, 249, 255); border-radius: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Only candidates who clear the Prelims exam are eligible for the Mains exam. The </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Mains examination consists of five papers in total, out of which </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-weight: bolder; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">General </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-weight: bolder; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Hindi</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> and the </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-weight: bolder; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Optional Subject</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> are qualifying in nature (their marks </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">are not added to the final merit). As per the latest changes, the Optional </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Subject paper is now of objective (MCQ) type.</span></div><table classname=\"editor-table\" style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin: 1rem 0px; width: 321.913px;\"><thead><tr style=\"background: rgb(248, 250, 252);\"><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Paper</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Subject</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Marks</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Duration</span></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Qualifying\nPaper</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">General\nHindi</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">100</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">3 Hours</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Paper – I</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">General\nStudies Paper 1</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">300</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">3 Hours</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Paper– II</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">General\nStudies Paper 2</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">300</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">3 Hours</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Paper– III</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Essay</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">300</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">3 Hours</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Qualifying\nPaper</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Optional\nSubject (Objective)</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">100</span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">3 Hours</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Candidates can choose one optional subject from a <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">list of 34 disciplines</font></span> while filling out the application form. These include Hindi, English, Urdu, Sanskrit, History, Geography, Public Administration, Political Science, Sociology, Economics, Law, Mathematics, various engineering branches, and more.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(51, 65, 85) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-style: normal;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">BPSC Mains Syllabus</font></span></span></blockquote><table classname=\"editor-table\" style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin: 1rem 0px; font-size: inherit; width: 284.8px;\"><thead><tr style=\"background: rgb(248, 250, 252);\"><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Subject</span></span></th><th style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(203, 213, 225); padding: 8px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Topics</span></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">General Hindi</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px;\"><ol><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Essay</span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Grammar </span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Syntax </span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Summarisation </span></font></li></ol></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">General Studies Paper 1</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px;\"><ol><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Indian culture</span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Modern History of India</span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Current  international and national events of importance</span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Statistical analysis, Diagrams and Graphs</span></font></li></ol><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\"></span></font></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">General Studies Paper 2</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px;\"><ol><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Indian Polity</span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Indian economy and geography of india</span></font></li><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Role and impact of science and technology in the development of India</span></font></li></ol></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Essay</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px;\"><ol><li><font face=\"Kokila, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.3333px;\">Moral and Philosophical essay</span></font></li><li>Hypothecal essay</li><li>Essay related to social, economic, political, religious and administrative issues</li><li>Essay related to self-reliant India and digital India</li><li>Essay related to problems, solutions and possibilities of Bihar</li><li>Essay related to popular proverbs and sayings of Bihar, ETC.</li></ol></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 15.6933px; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Optional Paper</span></span></td><td style=\"border-width: 1px; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); padding: 8px; font-size: 12px;\"><p data-pm-slice=\"0 0 []\"></p><ul><li>English Language and Literature\n</li><li>Urdu Language and Literature\n</li><li>Hindi Language and Literature\n</li><li>Persian Language and Literature\n</li><li>Arabic Language and Literature\n</li><li>Pali Language and Literature\n</li><li>Maithili Language and Literature\n</li><li>Bengali Language and Literature\n</li><li>Sanskrit Language and Literature\n</li><li>Chemistry\n</li><li>Sociology\n</li><li>Physics\n</li><li>Agriculture</li><li>Statistics</li><li>Botany</li><li>Zoology\n</li><li>Philosophy\n</li><li>Political Science and International Relations\n</li><li>Psychology\n</li><li>Public Administration\n</li><li>Labor and Social Welfare\n</li><li>Management\n</li><li>Mathematics\n</li><li>Mechanical Engineering\n</li><li>Geography\n</li><li>Geology\n</li><li>History\n</li><li>Law\n</li><li>Civil Engineering\n</li><li>Economics\n</li><li>Commerce and Accountancy\n</li><li>Electrical Engineering\n</li><li>Animal Husbandry and Veterinary Science\n</li><li>Anthropology\n</li></ul><p></p></td></tr></tbody></table><h1 style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(15, 23, 42) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">BPSC Interview (Personality Test):</font></span></h1><div><blockquote style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; color: rgb(51, 65, 85) !important;\">Candidates who clear the Mains examination are called for an interview<br>conducted by a board appointed by the Commission. The interview carries <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">120 marks</span> and is added to the final merit list.</blockquote><div><p data-pm-slice=\"0 0 []\"></p><ul><li>The board has access to a record of the candidate\'s career and interests as filled in the application form </li><li>The objective is to assess the candidate\'s personal suitability for a career in state services </li><li>Candidates are expected to be aware of current affairs within and outside their state </li><li>It is more of a purposeful conversation designed to assess mental alertness and analytical ability rather than a formal question-answer session.</li></ul><p></p><div style=\"border-width: 0px 0px 0px 6px; border-color: currentcolor currentcolor currentcolor rgb(245, 158, 11); margin: 1rem 0px; padding: 1.25rem; background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgb(15, 23, 42) 0%, rgb(30, 58, 138) 100%); border-radius: 16px; box-shadow: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.15) 0px 4px 12px;\"><div style=\"margin: 0px 0px 8px; font-size: 13px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;\"><h1 style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(15, 23, 42) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#f59e0b\">Preparation Tips:</font></span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: initial;\">      </span></h1></div><p data-pm-slice=\"0 0 []\"></p><ul><li><font color=\"#f43f5e\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Understand the exam pattern and syllabus thoroughly before starting preparation\n</span></font></li><li><font color=\"#f43f5e\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Build a strong base with NCERT books for History, Geography, Polity, and Economy\n</span></font></li><li><font color=\"#f43f5e\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Focus on Bihar-specific content such as the Bihar Economic Survey and Census reports\n</span></font></li><li><font color=\"#f43f5e\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Stay updated with current affairs through newspapers, PIB, and Yojana magazine\n</span></font></li><li><font color=\"#f43f5e\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Practice previous years\' question papers and mock tests regularly\n</span></font></li><li><font color=\"#f43f5e\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Give special emphasis to answer-writing practice for the Mains exam</span></font></li></ul><p></p></div><div><h2 style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; color: rgb(15, 23, 42) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><font color=\"#3b82f6\">Conclusion:</font></span></h2><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The BPSC exam is a multi-stage selection process that demands a clear understanding of the syllabus, consistent practice, and a strong grip on Bihar-related issues. Even though the Prelims exam is only qualifying in nature, it should be prepared for with the same seriousness as the Mains, since a strong foundation at this stage sets the tone for the following rounds.<o:p></o:p></p>\n\n        <div style=\"border-width: 1.5px 1.5px 1.5px 5px; border-color: rgb(253, 230, 138) rgb(253, 230, 138) rgb(253, 230, 138) rgb(217, 119, 6); margin: 1rem 0px; padding: 1.25rem; background: rgb(255, 251, 242); border-radius: 14px;\"><blockquote style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85) !important;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px; color: rgb(180, 83, 9); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;\">⭐<span style=\"font-style: normal;\"> </span></span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(238, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-style: normal;\">FAQs on BPSC Exam Pattern and Syllabus</span></blockquote><div style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(180, 83, 9); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;\">       </div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Q1. How often does BPSC conduct the exam?</span></span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-align: justify;\">BPSC conducts the Combined Competitive Examination annually, or as per the number of vacancies to be filled. The official notification for each cycle is released on the BPSC website <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><i><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">(</span></i></span><a href=\"https://bpsc.bihar.gov.in/\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><i><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">bpsc.bihar.gov.in</span></i></span></a><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><i><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\">),</span></i></span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\"> </span>and candidates should check it regularly for updates.</p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Q2. Are the marks scored in the Prelims exam counted in the final result?</span></span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-align: justify;\">No. The Preliminary exam only acts as a screening round to shortlist candidates for the Mains exam. Its marks are not added to the final merit list.<o:p></o:p></p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Q3. Is there negative marking in the BPSC Prelims exam?</span></span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-align: justify;\">Yes, there is a penalty of ⅓ mark for every incorrect answer in the Prelims exam, so candidates should attempt questions carefully and avoid guesswork.<o:p></o:p></p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Q4. Which stages\' marks are considered for the final BPSC merit list?</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-align: justify;\">Only the marks obtained in the Mains examination and the Interview are counted towards the final merit list. The Optional Subject and General Hindi papers in Mains are qualifying in nature\nand are not added to the merit.</p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Q5. What is the best way to prepare for the BPSC exam?</span></span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-align: justify;\">Candidates should build a strong conceptual base using NCERT books for History, Geography, Polity, and Economy, focus on Bihar-specific material such as the Bihar Economic Survey and Census\nreports, stay updated with current affairs through newspapers, PIB, and Yojana magazine, and regularly practice previous years\' papers, mock tests, and Mains answer-writing.</p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\">Q6. Where can candidates find reliable BPSC study material?</span></span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 32, 96);\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-align: justify;\">Along with NCERT books and official notifications, structured study material from experienced coaching institutes like FINAL ATTEMPT can be quite helpful in guiding candidates through every stage of the selection process.<o:p></o:p></p><div class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"center\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-align: center;\">\n<hr size=\"2\" width=\"100%\" align=\"center\"></div><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><i><span style=\"color: rgb(192, 0, 0);\">Note:</span></i></span><i><span style=\"color: rgb(192, 0, 0);\"> </span>The BPSC exam pattern and syllabus are subject to periodic revisions. Candidates should always refer to the </i><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><i><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 112, 192);\"><a href=\"https://bpsc.bihar.gov.in/\">official BPSC website</a></span></i></span><i><a href=\"https://bpsc.bihar.gov.in/\"> </a>for the latest notification.</i></p></div><p></p>\n      \n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px 0px 0in;\"><br></p>\n\n\n\n      </div><p></p></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n      \n\n\n\n\n      </div>', 'Beginner Strategy', '38fd709c-0102-417b-94a3-dd3e7b9bb0c9', NULL, 'https://youtu.be/o1ws85wi2zI', NULL, NULL, 0, 1, '2026-07-27 07:10:02.579', '2026-08-13 02:20:22.155');
INSERT INTO `Syllabus` (`id`, `examId`, `stage`, `version`, `mediaId`, `lastUpdated`, `description`, `isPublished`, `sortOrder`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`) VALUES
('2e2f80d3-e59d-40e0-886d-a73266be0673', '5cb632ed-d17d-4f2d-af21-8d5374782f5e', 'PRELIMS', '1.0', 'b8ee1ab5-a258-42e6-af81-90c14961bb75', '12/8/2026', '<h1>BPSC Syllabus and Exam Pattern 2026</h1><h2>About BPSC Exam</h2><p><strong>Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC)</strong> conducts the <strong>Combined Competitive Examination (CCE)</strong> every year to recruit candidates for various <strong>Group A and Group B posts</strong> under the Bihar Government.</p><p>Some of the major services/posts include:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Bihar Administrative Service (BAS)</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Bihar Police Service (BPS)</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Bihar Revenue Service (BRS)</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Bihar Financial Service (BFS)</strong></p></li></ul><p>If you are preparing for the <strong>BPSC Exam 2026</strong>, understanding the exact <strong>BPSC exam pattern and syllabus</strong> is one of the first and most important steps in your preparation.</p><p>This article covers the complete details of all three stages of the BPSC examination:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Preliminary Examination (Prelims)</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Main Examination (Mains)</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Interview / Personality Test</strong></p></li></ol><p>The syllabus and exam pattern have been presented in a simple and organized format to help BPSC aspirants understand the examination structure clearly.</p><hr><h1>BPSC Selection Process 2026</h1><p>The BPSC recruitment process is completed in <strong>three stages</strong>:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Examination Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Stage 1</strong></td><td>Preliminary Examination (Prelims) – Objective / MCQ Based</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Stage 2</strong></td><td>Main Examination (Mains) – Descriptive / Objective Type</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Stage 3</strong></td><td>Interview – Personality Test</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Quick Overview of BPSC Exam Pattern</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Type of Examination</th><th align=\"right\">Total Marks</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Prelims</strong></td><td>Objective – General Studies</td><td align=\"right\"><strong>150</strong></td><td><strong>2 Hours</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mains</strong></td><td>General Hindi (Qualifying) + GS Paper 1 + GS Paper 2 + Essay + Optional Subject (Qualifying)</td><td align=\"right\"><strong>1100</strong></td><td><strong>3 Hours for Each Paper</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Interview</strong></td><td>Personality Test</td><td align=\"right\"><strong>120</strong></td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table><blockquote><p><strong>Important:</strong> The <strong>Prelims examination is purely qualifying/screening in nature</strong>. Its marks are not counted in the final merit list. The Prelims examination is used to shortlist candidates for the Mains examination.</p></blockquote><p>The <strong>final selection</strong> is based on the marks obtained in the <strong>Mains Examination and Interview</strong>.</p><hr><h1>BPSC Eligibility Criteria 2026</h1><p>Candidates appearing for the BPSC examination must fulfill the prescribed eligibility conditions.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Eligibility Criteria</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Nationality</strong></td><td>Indian Citizen</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Age Limit</strong></td><td>Generally, <strong>20 to 37 years</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Age Relaxation</strong></td><td>Applicable as per category and post</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Educational Qualification</strong></td><td>Graduate degree from a recognized university</td></tr></tbody></table><blockquote><p><strong>Note:</strong> Eligibility conditions may vary depending on the post and the particular BPSC recruitment notification. Candidates should always check the latest official notification for exact eligibility requirements.</p></blockquote><hr><h1>BPSC Prelims Exam Pattern 2026</h1><p>The <strong>BPSC Preliminary Examination</strong> consists of a <strong>single General Studies paper</strong>.</p><h3>BPSC Prelims Exam Pattern</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Particular</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Name of Exam</strong></td><td>Combined Competitive Examination (General Studies)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Number of Papers</strong></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total Marks</strong></td><td>150</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mode of Examination</strong></td><td>Offline (OMR Based)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Duration</strong></td><td>2 Hours</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Number of Questions</strong></td><td>150</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nature of Questions</strong></td><td>Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Negative Marking</strong></td><td>⅓ mark per wrong answer</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Important Points About BPSC Prelims</h3><ul><li><p>The Prelims consists of <strong>one General Studies paper</strong>.</p></li><li><p>The paper carries <strong>150 marks</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Candidates get <strong>2 hours</strong> to complete the examination.</p></li><li><p>The examination is conducted in <strong>offline OMR-based mode</strong>.</p></li><li><p>There are <strong>150 objective-type questions</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>⅓ mark is deducted for every incorrect answer</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Prelims marks are <strong>not counted in the final merit list</strong>.</p></li><li><p>The examination is primarily used as a <strong>screening stage for the Mains examination</strong>.</p></li></ul><hr><h1>BPSC Prelims Syllabus 2026</h1><p>The BPSC Prelims General Studies paper covers various subjects related to <strong>General Science, Current Affairs, History, Geography, Indian Polity, Economy, Indian National Movement and General Mental Ability</strong>.</p><h2>BPSC Prelims Syllabus – Subject Wise</h2><h3>1. General Science</h3><p>Questions are based on a general understanding of science derived from <strong>everyday observation and experience</strong>.</p><p>The syllabus broadly covers:</p><ul><li><p>Physics</p></li><li><p>Chemistry</p></li><li><p>Biology</p></li><li><p>Technological developments</p></li><li><p>Basic scientific concepts related to everyday life</p></li></ul><p>No specialized subject knowledge is generally required.</p><h3>2. Current Affairs</h3><p>Questions may be asked from events and developments of <strong>national and international importance</strong>, including:</p><ul><li><p>Awards</p></li><li><p>Sports</p></li><li><p>Government schemes</p></li><li><p>National developments</p></li><li><p>International developments</p></li><li><p>Recent developments in Science and Technology</p></li></ul><h3>3. History</h3><p>The syllabus covers the <strong>History of India and Bihar</strong>, including a broad understanding of:</p><ul><li><p>Ancient Indian History</p></li><li><p>Medieval Indian History</p></li><li><p>Modern Indian History</p></li><li><p>Important historical developments in Bihar</p></li></ul><p>Special emphasis is given to <strong>Bihar-related history</strong>.</p><h3>4. Geography</h3><p>The Geography syllabus covers the <strong>physical, social and economic geography of India and Bihar</strong>.</p><p>Important areas include:</p><ul><li><p>Physical geography</p></li><li><p>Social geography</p></li><li><p>Economic geography</p></li><li><p>Indian agriculture</p></li><li><p>Natural resources</p></li><li><p>River systems</p></li><li><p>Geographical divisions of Bihar</p></li></ul><h3>5. Indian Polity</h3><p>Important areas include:</p><ul><li><p>Indian political system</p></li><li><p>Panchayati Raj</p></li><li><p>Community development</p></li><li><p>Planning in India</p></li><li><p>Planning and development in Bihar</p></li></ul><h3>6. Economy</h3><p>The syllabus includes:</p><ul><li><p>Indian Economy</p></li><li><p>Economy of Bihar</p></li><li><p>Economic developments in India since Independence</p></li><li><p>Economic developments in Bihar since Independence</p></li></ul><h3>7. Indian National Movement</h3><p>This section covers the <strong>nature and growth of nationalism in the 19th century</strong> and the role of Bihar in India\'s freedom struggle.</p><p>Important topics include:</p><ul><li><p>Revolt of 1857</p></li><li><p>Champaran Satyagraha</p></li><li><p>Birsa Movement</p></li><li><p>Quit India Movement of 1942</p></li><li><p>Role of Bihar in India\'s freedom struggle</p></li></ul><h3>8. General Mental Ability</h3><p>Questions are designed to test:</p><ul><li><p>Logical reasoning</p></li><li><p>Problem-solving ability</p></li><li><p>Analytical ability</p></li></ul><hr><h1>BPSC Mains Exam Pattern 2026</h1><p>Candidates who qualify the Preliminary Examination become eligible to appear for the <strong>BPSC Main Examination</strong>.</p><p>The Mains examination consists of <strong>five papers</strong>. Out of these, <strong>General Hindi</strong> and the <strong>Optional Subject</strong> are qualifying in nature, meaning their marks are not added to the final merit.</p><p>As per the latest changes, the <strong>Optional Subject paper is of objective (MCQ) type</strong>.</p><h2>BPSC Mains Exam Pattern</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Paper</th><th>Subject</th><th align=\"right\">Marks</th><th>Duration</th><th>Nature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Qualifying Paper</strong></td><td>General Hindi</td><td align=\"right\">100</td><td>3 Hours</td><td>Qualifying</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Paper – I</strong></td><td>General Studies Paper 1</td><td align=\"right\">300</td><td>3 Hours</td><td>Merit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Paper – II</strong></td><td>General Studies Paper 2</td><td align=\"right\">300</td><td>3 Hours</td><td>Merit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Paper – III</strong></td><td>Essay</td><td align=\"right\">300</td><td>3 Hours</td><td>Merit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Qualifying Paper</strong></td><td>Optional Subject (Objective)</td><td align=\"right\">100</td><td>3 Hours</td><td>Qualifying</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Total Mains Marks</h3><p>The BPSC Mains examination carries a total of <strong>1100 marks</strong>, including the qualifying papers.</p><p>However, the <strong>General Hindi and Optional Subject papers are qualifying in nature</strong>, and their marks are not added to the final merit.</p><hr><h1>BPSC Mains Optional Subjects</h1><p>Candidates can choose <strong>one optional subject</strong> from the list of <strong>34 disciplines</strong> while filling out the application form.</p><p>The available optional subjects include:</p><ol><li><p>English Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Urdu Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Hindi Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Persian Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Arabic Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Pali Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Maithili Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Bengali Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Sanskrit Language and Literature</p></li><li><p>Chemistry</p></li><li><p>Sociology</p></li><li><p>Physics</p></li><li><p>Agriculture</p></li><li><p>Statistics</p></li><li><p>Botany</p></li><li><p>Zoology</p></li><li><p>Philosophy</p></li><li><p>Political Science and International Relations</p></li><li><p>Psychology</p></li><li><p>Public Administration</p></li><li><p>Labor and Social Welfare</p></li><li><p>Management</p></li><li><p>Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Mechanical Engineering</p></li><li><p>Geography</p></li><li><p>Geology</p></li><li><p>History</p></li><li><p>Law</p></li><li><p>Civil Engineering</p></li><li><p>Economics</p></li><li><p>Commerce and Accountancy</p></li><li><p>Electrical Engineering</p></li><li><p>Animal Husbandry and Veterinary Science</p></li><li><p>Anthropology</p></li></ol><hr><h1>BPSC Mains Syllabus 2026</h1><p>The BPSC Mains syllabus is divided into <strong>General Hindi, General Studies Paper 1, General Studies Paper 2, Essay and Optional Subject</strong>.</p><h2>General Hindi</h2><p>The General Hindi paper covers the following areas:</p><ol><li><p>Essay</p></li><li><p>Grammar</p></li><li><p>Syntax</p></li><li><p>Summarisation</p></li></ol><hr><h2>General Studies Paper 1</h2><p>BPSC Mains General Studies Paper 1 broadly covers the following areas:</p><ol><li><p>Indian Culture</p></li><li><p>Modern History of India</p></li><li><p>Current International and National Events of Importance</p></li><li><p>Statistical Analysis, Diagrams and Graphs</p></li></ol><hr><h2>General Studies Paper 2</h2><p>BPSC Mains General Studies Paper 2 covers:</p><ol><li><p>Indian Polity</p></li><li><p>Indian Economy and Geography of India</p></li><li><p>Role and Impact of Science and Technology in the Development of India</p></li></ol><hr><h1>BPSC Mains Essay Syllabus</h1><p>The Essay paper covers a wide range of social, economic, political, philosophical and administrative themes.</p><p>Important areas include:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Moral and Philosophical Essays</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Hypothetical Essays</strong></p></li><li><p>Essays related to <strong>Social, Economic, Political, Religious and Administrative Issues</strong></p></li><li><p>Essays related to <strong>Self-Reliant India and Digital India</strong></p></li><li><p>Essays related to <strong>Problems, Solutions and Possibilities of Bihar</strong></p></li><li><p>Essays related to <strong>Popular Proverbs and Sayings of Bihar</strong></p></li><li><p>Other relevant contemporary and issue-based topics</p></li></ol><hr><h1>BPSC Interview / Personality Test</h1><p>Candidates who successfully clear the <strong>BPSC Mains Examination</strong> are called for the <strong>Interview / Personality Test</strong> conducted by a board appointed by the Commission.</p><p>The interview carries <strong>120 marks</strong>, which are added to the final merit list.</p><h3>Important Features of the BPSC Interview</h3><ul><li><p>The interview board has access to the candidate\'s <strong>career record and interests</strong> as provided in the application form.</p></li><li><p>The objective is to assess the candidate\'s <strong>personal suitability for a career in state services</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Candidates are expected to remain aware of <strong>current affairs within and outside Bihar</strong>.</p></li><li><p>The interview is more of a <strong>purposeful conversation</strong> designed to assess:</p><ul><li><p>Mental alertness</p></li><li><p>Analytical ability</p></li><li><p>Personality</p></li><li><p>Awareness</p></li><li><p>Suitability for public service</p></li></ul></li></ul><hr><h1>BPSC Preparation Tips</h1><p>A well-planned preparation strategy is essential for success in the BPSC examination.</p><h3>1. Understand the Exam Pattern and Syllabus</h3><p>Before beginning preparation, understand the <strong>complete BPSC syllabus and exam pattern</strong> thoroughly. This helps you identify important subjects and prioritize your preparation.</p><h3>2. Build a Strong Foundation</h3><p>Build a strong conceptual foundation using <strong>NCERT books</strong> for:</p><ul><li><p>History</p></li><li><p>Geography</p></li><li><p>Polity</p></li><li><p>Economy</p></li></ul><h3>3. Focus on Bihar-Specific Content</h3><p>Bihar-specific preparation is extremely important for BPSC aspirants.</p><p>Give special attention to resources such as:</p><ul><li><p>Bihar Economic Survey</p></li><li><p>Census Reports</p></li><li><p>Bihar-specific history</p></li><li><p>Bihar geography</p></li><li><p>Bihar economy</p></li><li><p>Bihar government schemes and developments</p></li></ul><h3>4. Stay Updated with Current Affairs</h3><p>Regularly follow current affairs through reliable sources such as:</p><ul><li><p>Newspapers</p></li><li><p>PIB</p></li><li><p>Yojana Magazine</p></li><li><p>Government reports and publications</p></li></ul><p>Give special attention to <strong>Bihar-related current affairs</strong> along with national and international developments.</p><h3>5. Practice Previous Year Question Papers</h3><p>Solve <strong>BPSC Previous Year Question Papers (PYQs)</strong> regularly.</p><p>PYQs help you understand:</p><ul><li><p>Question trends</p></li><li><p>Important topics</p></li><li><p>Difficulty level</p></li><li><p>Repeated themes</p></li><li><p>Examination pattern</p></li></ul><h3>6. Practice Mock Tests</h3><p>Regularly attempt mock tests to improve:</p><ul><li><p>Speed</p></li><li><p>Accuracy</p></li><li><p>Time management</p></li><li><p>Question selection</p></li><li><p>Exam temperament</p></li></ul><h3>7. Give Special Emphasis to Mains Answer Writing</h3><p>For Mains preparation, develop a consistent <strong>answer-writing practice</strong>.</p><p>Focus on:</p><ul><li><p>Structure</p></li><li><p>Content</p></li><li><p>Introduction</p></li><li><p>Body</p></li><li><p>Conclusion</p></li><li><p>Relevant examples</p></li><li><p>Bihar-specific dimensions</p></li><li><p>Facts and data</p></li><li><p>Time management</p></li></ul><hr><h1>BPSC Exam Pattern: Prelims vs Mains vs Interview</h1><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Prelims</th><th>Mains</th><th>Interview</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Purpose</strong></td><td>Screening / Shortlisting</td><td>Merit</td><td>Personality Assessment</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Type</strong></td><td>Objective</td><td>Descriptive + Objective Qualifying Paper</td><td>Personality Test</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Marks</strong></td><td>150</td><td>1100</td><td>120</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Duration</strong></td><td>2 Hours</td><td>3 Hours per Paper</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Negative Marking</strong></td><td>⅓ mark per wrong answer</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Marks Added to Final Merit</strong></td><td>No</td><td>Yes, except qualifying papers</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h1>Conclusion</h1><p>The <strong>BPSC examination</strong> is a multi-stage selection process that demands a clear understanding of the syllabus, consistent practice and a strong grip on <strong>Bihar-related issues</strong>.\n\n</p><p>Although the <strong>Prelims examination is qualifying in nature</strong>, it should be prepared for with the same seriousness as the Mains because clearing Prelims is essential for reaching the next stage.\n\n</p><p>A strong foundation during Prelims preparation can also significantly benefit your Mains preparation. Therefore, candidates should combine <strong>conceptual understanding, Bihar-specific preparation, current affairs, PYQs, mock tests and Mains answer-writing practice</strong> throughout their preparation journey.\n\n</p><p>Understanding the <strong>BPSC Syllabus and Exam Pattern 2026</strong> is the first step toward building a focused and effective preparation strategy.</p><hr><h1>⭐ FAQs on BPSC Exam Pattern and Syllabus</h1><h2>Q1. How often does BPSC conduct the exam?</h2><p>BPSC conducts the <strong>Combined Competitive Examination</strong> annually, or as per the number of vacancies to be filled.</p><p>The official notification for each examination cycle is released on the <strong>BPSC website</strong>, and candidates should regularly check the official website for the latest updates.</p><h2>Q2. Are the marks scored in the BPSC Prelims counted in the final result?</h2><p><strong>No.</strong></p><p>The Preliminary Examination acts as a <strong>screening round</strong> to shortlist candidates for the Mains Examination. The marks obtained in Prelims are <strong>not added to the final merit list</strong>.</p><h2>Q3. Is there negative marking in the BPSC Prelims exam?</h2><p><strong>Yes.</strong></p><p>There is a penalty of <strong>⅓ mark for every incorrect answer</strong> in the Prelims examination.</p><p>Therefore, candidates should attempt questions carefully and avoid unnecessary guesswork.</p><h2>Q4. Which stages\' marks are considered for the final BPSC merit list?</h2><p>The final merit is based on the marks obtained in the <strong>Mains Examination and Interview</strong>.</p><p>The <strong>General Hindi and Optional Subject papers</strong> in Mains are qualifying in nature and their marks are not added to the final merit.</p><h2>Q5. What is the best way to prepare for the BPSC exam?</h2><p>Candidates should:</p><ul><li><p>Build a strong conceptual foundation using NCERT books for History, Geography, Polity and Economy.</p></li><li><p>Focus on Bihar-specific material such as the Bihar Economic Survey and Census reports.</p></li><li><p>Stay updated with current affairs through newspapers, PIB and Yojana Magazine.</p></li><li><p>Regularly practice previous years\' question papers.</p></li><li><p>Attempt mock tests.</p></li><li><p>Develop consistent Mains answer-writing practice.</p></li><li><p>Pay special attention to Bihar-specific issues and current affairs.</p></li></ul><h2>Q6. Where can candidates find reliable BPSC study material?</h2><p>Candidates can refer to <strong>NCERT books, official government reports, BPSC notifications, previous year question papers and other reliable study resources</strong>.</p><p>Structured study material from experienced coaching institutes can also be helpful in providing organized guidance and preparation support for different stages of the BPSC examination.</p><hr><h2>Important Note</h2><p><strong>The BPSC exam pattern and syllabus are subject to periodic revisions.</strong></p><p>Candidates should always refer to the <strong>latest official BPSC notification and official website</strong> for the most accurate and updated information regarding:</p><ul><li><p>Examination pattern</p></li><li><p>Syllabus</p></li><li><p>Eligibility</p></li><li><p>Vacancies</p></li><li><p>Age limit</p></li><li><p>Optional subjects</p></li><li><p>Important dates</p></li><li><p>Selection process</p></li></ul><p><strong>Official BPSC Website:</strong> bpsc.bihar.gov.in</p>', 1, 0, '2026-08-12 02:29:28.912', '2026-08-12 02:29:28.912');
